  "name": "CYFRA (Ca)21-1 LUNG CANCER",
  "code": "1750",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong data-start=\"63\" data-end=\"77\">CYFRA 21-1</strong> is a <strong data-start=\"83\" data-end=\"99\">tumor marker</strong> that measures a <strong data-start=\"116\" data-end=\"146\">fragment of cytokeratin 19</strong>, a structural protein found in epithelial cells. It is commonly elevated in <strong data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"264\">non-small cell lung carcinoma (NSCLC)</strong>, especially the <strong data-start=\"281\" data-end=\"306\">squamous cell subtype</strong>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Level</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Possible Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal (&lt;3.3 ng/mL)</strong></td>\n<td>No significant elevation; less likely to have NSCLC, but not ruled out</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Mild elevation (3.3&ndash;10 ng/mL)</strong></td>\n<td>May be seen in <strong>early-stage NSCLC</strong>, <strong>benign lung disease</strong>, or <strong>other cancers</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Marked elevation (&gt;10 ng/mL)</strong></td>\n<td>Suggestive of <strong>advanced NSCLC</strong>, especially <strong>squamous cell carcinoma</strong> subtype</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1528\" data-end=\"1579\"><strong data-start=\"1532\" data-end=\"1579\">Conditions Where CYFRA 21-1 May Be Elevated</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1580\" data-end=\"1850\">\n<li data-start=\"1580\" data-end=\"1650\">\n<p data-start=\"1582\" data-end=\"1650\"><strong data-start=\"1582\" data-end=\"1623\">Non-small cell lung carcinoma (NSCLC)</strong> &ndash; especially squamous cell</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1651\" data-end=\"1717\">\n<p data-start=\"1653\" data-end=\"1717\">Other epithelial cancers: <strong data-start=\"1679\" data-end=\"1690\">bladder</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1692\" data-end=\"1702\">cervix</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1704\" data-end=\"1717\">esophagus</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1718\" data-end=\"1792\">\n<p data-start=\"1720\" data-end=\"1792\"><strong data-start=\"1720\" data-end=\"1744\">Benign lung diseases</strong>: tuberculosis, pneumonia, COPD (mild elevation)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1793\" data-end=\"1850\">\n<p data-start=\"1795\" data-end=\"1850\"><strong data-start=\"1795\" data-end=\"1826\">Liver or kidney dysfunction</strong> (rare false elevations)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
